<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Importance of Panama in Global Trade – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Panama's Role in the World</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> The Importance of Panama in Global Trade</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Present an analysis of a current issue, local or global. Interactive: Conduct interviews on various topics, including current events, academic topics, and past experiences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can present an analysis of the Panama Canal's impact during the 2023 drought to explain decisions (e.g., "New regulations were imposed to limit the number of daily crossings to conserve water.")
                Can conduct interviews on global trade topics, asking about the Canal's effects on trade (e.g., "How has the Panama Canal impacted global trade?" "If Panama had not built the Canal, global trade would have faced significant challenges in the early 20th century.")
                Can summarize responses from interviews, focusing on the economic impact of the Canal (e.g., "It was explained that without the Panama Canal, shipping would have been slower and more costly.")</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e6ea; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e6ea; color: #1a5276; width: 60%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e6ea; color: #1a5276; width: 10%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher begins by showing images of congested ships waiting at the Panama Canal and a chart illustrating the impact of the 2023 drought on Canal traffic. Students are asked to briefly discuss in pairs: "What do these images and data tell us about the current situation of the Panama Canal and its influence on global trade?" (2-3 minutes). The teacher then elicits a few responses, focusing on vocabulary like 'congestion,' 'delays,' 'shipping,' 'traffic,' and 'impactful.' For example, a student might say, "The traffic in the Canal has been causing significant delays."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models sentences using target grammar and vocabulary relevant to the images and discussion. For instance: "The Canal has been impacting global trade significantly due to recent drought-related regulations." (Present Perfect Continuous, 'impacting,' 'global trade'). "If the Canal had not adjusted its operations, the situation would have been even more challenging." (Third Conditional, 'adjusted,' 'operations,' 'challenging'). The teacher emphasizes the pronunciation of words like "global" /oʊ/ and "environmental" /ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.təl/, highlighting the long vowel sound and reduced vowels in multisyllabic words, asking students to repeat. "The Canal has been managed by the Panama Canal Authority since 1999, overseeing its global relationships." (Passive Voice, 'managed,' 'overseeing,' 'global relationships').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say, 'New regulations were imposed to limit daily crossings,' who imposed the regulations? The Canal Authority or the ships?" (Expected: The Canal Authority – checks understanding of passive voice).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say, 'If Panama had not built the Canal, global trade would have faced challenges,' did Panama build the Canal?" (Expected: Yes – checks understanding of third conditional for past hypothetical).</li>
                </ul>
                The teacher also checks understanding of key vocabulary such as 'congestion' and 'efficiency' by asking students to give an example of each in the context of the Canal.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher presents a short audio clip (approx. 1.5 minutes) from a news report or an expert interview discussing the recent challenges faced by the Panama Canal due to the 2023 drought and the decisions made by the Canal Authority. The report will naturally integrate the target grammar (passive voice, conditionals, present perfect continuous) and vocabulary (e.g., 'operation,' 'efficiency,' 'investments,' 'environmental concerns,' 'government,' 'authority,' 'routes,' 'costs,' 'delays').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Authentic audio recording of a news report or interview excerpt on Panama Canal operations and drought impact (genre: news report, register: formal/academic, format: audio/spoken text).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Comprehend short, complex spoken texts on current issues related to global trade and Panama's role, identifying key arguments and specific details.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the audio twice.
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main challenge discussed in the report regarding the Panama Canal?" "Who is primarily affected by this situation?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> (e.g., "The number of daily crossings has been increased due to high demand." - False) "Environmental groups have raised concerns about the Canal's long-term sustainability." - True.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match problems (e.g., 'drought,' 'increased costs') with solutions/consequences (e.g., 'limited crossings,' 'longer routes').</li>
                </ul>
                After each listening, students briefly share their answers with a partner, promoting immediate speaking engagement.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice using the passive voice, second and third conditionals, and the present perfect continuous, along with key vocabulary related to global trade and the Panama Canal.
                Vocabulary: Panama Canal, operation, traffic, congestion, routes, shipping, trade, infrastructure, efficiency, costs, delays, government, investments, environmental groups, ecosystems, authority, global relationships, influence, construction, future, operate, manage, monitor, prevent, invest, enhance, raise concerns, affect, complete, speculate, improve, face, delay, impact, influence, navigate, control, oversee, transport, adjust, global, expensive, efficient, long-term, environmental, local, impactful, sustainable, monitored, influential, completed, significant, costly, delayed, congested, speculative.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Sentence Completion (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher displays incomplete sentences on the board related to the Canal's impact. Students work individually to complete them orally, focusing on the target grammar. The teacher calls on students to read their completed sentences aloud, providing immediate feedback on accuracy and pronunciation.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 1: "Since the drought, the number of ships _______ (limit) to ensure water conservation." (Expected: has been limited / is being limited)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 2: "If the government ______ (not invest) in infrastructure, the Canal's efficiency ______ (not improve) much." (Expected: hadn't invested, wouldn't have improved)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 3: "Global trade ______ (face) significant delays if alternative routes _______ (not find)." (Expected: would face, were not found)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Chain Speaking (Semi-Controlled Practice):</b> Students sit in a circle. The teacher starts a sentence (e.g., "The Panama Canal has been improving global trade..."). The first student adds a phrase using a target grammatical structure or vocabulary word. The next student repeats the full sentence and adds another phrase. This continues around the circle. Example: "The Panama Canal has been improving global trade... and if it had not been constructed, shipping costs would have been much higher." The teacher prompts for variety in grammar structures (passive, conditionals, present perfect continuous) and vocabulary (e.g., 'environmental concerns,' 'investments,' 'efficiency,' 'influence').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>"What If?" Pair Discussion (Semi-Controlled Practice):</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher provides hypothetical prompts related to the Canal. Students take turns asking and answering, using second and third conditionals. The teacher circulates, listening for accurate usage and providing support.
                        <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 1: "What if the Panama Canal had never been built?" (Student A: "If the Panama Canal had never been built, global trade would have been significantly slower and more costly.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 2: "What if the drought continues for another year?" (Student B: "If the drought continued, more stringent regulations would be imposed, affecting global shipping routes.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 3: "What if Panama decides to invest heavily in a new, even wider canal?" (Student A: "If Panama decided to invest, its global influence would be enhanced, but environmental groups might raise concerns about ecosystems.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Panama's Role in the World".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task: "Canal Impact Interview"</b>
                Students work in pairs. One student plays the role of an "Expert on Global Trade" (e.g., from the Panama Canal Authority or an environmental group), and the other plays a "News Reporter" interviewing the expert about the Panama Canal's current situation and future outlook, particularly focusing on the 2023 drought and its broader impact. Both roles are given a card with bullet points to guide their discussion and ensure they use target vocabulary and grammatical structures. (e.g., Expert card: Discuss decisions made by the authority, environmental concerns, future investments. Reporter card: Ask about current challenges, hypothetical scenarios, global relationships.)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Role-play interview simulation (5 minutes per pair). Each pair will present their interview to another pair or a small group.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. The teacher explains the roles and provides prompt cards to each student.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. Students have 2-3 minutes to prepare their questions/answers, ensuring they integrate passive voice, second/third conditionals, and present perfect continuous, as well as the specified vocabulary. They are encouraged to use phrases like: "How has the Panama Canal been impacting global trade?" "If Panama had not built the Canal, global trade would have faced significant challenges..." "It was explained that without the Panama Canal, shipping would have been slower..." They also focus on respectful language about Panama's role and appropriate trade-related terms.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. Pairs conduct their interviews, focusing on fluency and interaction. The teacher circulates, monitoring for language use and providing discreet support.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">4. After 5 minutes, pairs switch roles and repeat the activity.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">5. (Optional, if time permits) Selected pairs perform a portion of their interview for the whole class, or pairs summarize their partner's interview to another group.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on speaking performance. Peer assessment (optional, brief rubric).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their "Canal Impact Interview" (from Stage 4) to another pair or small group. The teacher observes specific pairs using a checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (including /oʊ/ and multisyllabic words like 'environmental,' 'impactful').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'congestion,' 'efficiency,' 'investments,' 'ecosystems').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of passive voice (e.g., "Decisions were made...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of second and third conditionals (e.g., "If this happened, it would...", "If it had happened, it would have...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Present Perfect Continuous (e.g., "The Canal has been facing...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of analysis and explanation of ideas.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective collaborative interaction with partner.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of respectful and academic language related to global trade.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an individual exit ticket with these prompts:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new vocabulary word or phrase I used successfully today was..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I found it challenging to use ______ (grammar point, e.g., third conditional) accurately. I need more practice with..."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">7-8 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident do I feel now discussing the Panama Canal's impact on global trade and expressing hypothetical ideas?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific aspect of my speaking (e.g., fluency, vocabulary, grammar accuracy) improved most today, and what still needs attention?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific speaking activities worked best to engage students and promote the use of target grammar and vocabulary? The 'What If?' pair discussion seemed particularly effective for conditionals."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next speaking tasks or to reinforce specific grammar points (e.g., more structured prompts for present perfect continuous)? Some students struggled with the reduced vowels in multisyllabic words like 'environmental,' requiring further pronunciation practice."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can the fluency of students be further supported in future speaking lessons?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on speaking about the Panama Canal's impact and hypothetical scenarios. In Lesson 4, students will transition these ideas into written form, crafting descriptive paragraphs or short reports based on the discussions and information gathered today, focusing on written accuracy and coherence using the same target vocabulary and grammar structures. This will help them consolidate their understanding and express complex ideas in writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>